user*  is a programming language developed by Google to be used for Google’s internal purposes only. It was first released to the public in May 2010. It was designed with a focus on speed and flexibility, and as such, it has been criticized by some for having a less rigorous set of syntax and conventions compared to other languages, as well as a less powerful standard library. 

==Background==
Google originally developed the GoogleScript programming language for internal Google use. GoogleScript is a JavaScript-like scripting language that allows developers to manipulate web page structure and behavior.

==Syntax==
Auser uses the same operators and functions found in JavaScript. Some functions from Google's Google Apps Script are also included with Auser. For example, if you wanted to run the following piece of Auser code, it would run the following piece of Google Apps Script code:

function myAuserFunction(){
  var myAuserObject = auser('myGoogleAppsScriptObject');
  myAuserObject.execute('myGoogleAppsScriptFunction');
}

It translates to the following piece of Google Apps Script code:

function myAuserFunction(){
  var myGoogleAppsScriptObject = Utils['myGoogleAppsScriptObject'];
  myGoogleAppsScriptObject.execute('myGoogleAppsScriptFunction');
}

==Features==
*Auser can be used directly within JavaScript
